From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 07:09:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(session_search): find the chat's finished subagents and
 match long queries

A finished delegate_task child's transcript never reached its parent,
only the summary did, yet discovery hid it as the same lineage. Only a
running child is live context. A child with an end stamp (any reason),
or an unended one with no write for 30 minutes (its gateway died), is now
discoverable from its parent, siblings and grandchildren. Other chats'
subagents stay hidden.

FTS5 ANDs every word, so a long query whose words were spread over
several messages found nothing. When fewer sessions than the limit
contain every word, sessions matching any word (bm25 order) fill the
rest after the exact matches. Results carry match=all_terms/any_terms,
and the payload has match_mode and a note.

An empty result now says how many matches were in the chat's live
context and were not shown.
